Class AIRunService:
- validate operation_context by run_type, including optional `recommendation_count` bounds for `recommend_full_build`
- create run metadata with cache keys and optional bound session ownership checks
- append debug log entries when an AI run is created, including cache resolution and explicit cache-hit records even when no provider LLM call is needed
- derive one deterministic LLM debug filename from the run start timestamp plus the last four characters of run_id, then carry that file name together with session_id/run_id through every LLM debug scope so the full trace stays in one log file
- short-circuit compatible strong cache hits while still updating transcripts, leaderboard, and metrics
- bypass stale `game_status` cache payloads that do not contain the current hero stat-profile fields
- execute the LangGraph pipeline with model selection derived from combined `provider:model_name` config refs, injected baseline/reference/calibration/session context, optional precomputed tool state, and a dedicated slug-selector model when configured
- post-process completed AI text with the current catalog and response preferences so canonical slugs inside user-visible strings become localized names while machine-readable slug fields stay unchanged
- route `explain_slot` through the fixed OpenAI `gpt-5.4` model and reject old cached slot explanations that do not contain item-letter ratings
- write ai_runs metadata and artifacts including prompt payloads plus tool traces/facts
- update cache, leaderboard, transcripts, metrics, and structured logs after completion
- expose background streaming execution that first collects tool context, streams localized preview text with slug-safe buffering, then finalizes structured JSON
